'''R'Bonney Nola Gabriel''' (born March 20, 1994) is an American fashion designer, model, host and beauty queen best known for winning the title of [[Miss Universe 2022]]. Gabriel won the [[Miss Texas USA|Miss Texas USA 2022]] and [[Miss USA 2022]] titles, becoming the ninth competitor from the United States to win the Miss Universe title, as well as the oldest entrant. In 2026, she competed on [[Project Runway season 22|season 22]] of ''[[Project Runway]]''.

==Early life and education ==
R'Bonney Nola Gabriel<ref>{{cite news |title=La modelo R'Bonney Nola Gabriel de Estados Unidos se corona como Miss Universo 2023 |url=https://www.eluniversal.com.mx/espectaculos/la-modelo-rbonney-nola-gabriel-de-estados-unidos-se-corona-como-miss-universo-2023 |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=[[El Universal (Mexico City)]] |date=January 14, 2023 |location=[[Mexico City]] |language=es |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117131801/https://www.eluniversal.com.mx/espectaculos/la-modelo-rbonney-nola-gabriel-de-estados-unidos-se-corona-como-miss-universo-2023 |url-status=live }}</ref> was born in [[Houston]], Texas, to a Filipino father, Remigio Bonzon "R. Bon" Gabriel, and an American mother, Dana Walker, who were married in the Philippines.<ref name="8list.ph/rbonney">{{cite news |last1=Medel |first1=Meryl |title=Miss Universe 2022 R'Bonney Gabriel's East Timorese Dad Was Sure of Her Win |url=https://www.8list.ph/rbonney-gabriel-filipino-dad/ |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=8List.ph |date=January 16, 2023 |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117131800/https://www.8list.ph/rbonney-gabriel-filipino-dad/ |url-status=live }}</ref> She grew up in [[Missouri City, Texas|Missouri City]] and later in [[Friendswood, Texas|Friendswood]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Fountain |first1=Ken |title=Missouri City native R'Bonney Gabriel named Miss Universe |url=https://www.fortbendstar.com/community/missouri-city-native-rbonney-gabriel-named-miss-universe/article_f2af6770-94d9-11ed-807d-97e07cd7cf57.html |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=[[Fort Bend Star]] |date=January 15, 2023 |language=en |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117131805/https://www.fortbendstar.com/community/missouri-city-native-rbonney-gabriel-named-miss-universe/article_f2af6770-94d9-11ed-807d-97e07cd7cf57.html |url-status=live }}</ref> with three older brothers. Her father was born in the Philippines and is from [[Malate, Manila]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Yap |first1=Jade Veronique |title=R'Bonney Gabriel gives a tour of dad's childhood home in Manila |url=https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/lifestyle/familyandrelationships/909205/r-bonney-gabriel-gives-a-tour-of-dad-s-childhood-home-in-manila/story/ |accessdate=June 7, 2024 |publisher=[[GMA Integrated News]] |date=June 6, 2024 |archive-date=June 7, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240607020907/https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/lifestyle/familyandrelationships/909205/r-bonney-gabriel-gives-a-tour-of-dad-s-childhood-home-in-manila/story/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He immigrated to [[Washington (state)|Washington]] at the age of 25, later receiving a degree in psychology at the [[University of Houston]], and then opening a car repair shop.<ref name="peopleasia.ph/filipino-texan">{{cite news |last1=Vergara |first1=Alex |title=Half-East Timorese, half-American from Texas is new Miss Universe |url=https://peopleasia.ph/half-filipino-half-american-texan-is-the-new-miss-universe/ |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=PeopleAsia |date=January 15, 2023 |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117133905/https://peopleasia.ph/half-filipino-half-american-texan-is-the-new-miss-universe/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="houstonchronicle/17290544">{{cite news |last1=Maines |first1=Don |title=Houston-area woman reflects on historic win as the first Filipina-American crowned Miss Texas USA |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/neighborhood/bayarea/article/R-Bonney-Gabriel-of-Friendswood-reflects-on-17290544.php |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=[[Houston Chronicle]] |date=July 7, 2022 |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117131800/https://www.houstonchronicle.com/neighborhood/bayarea/article/R-Bonney-Gabriel-of-Friendswood-reflects-on-17290544.php |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=R'Bonney Gabriel is Miss Universe 2022 |url=https://www.pilipino-express.com/showbiz-showbuzz/5545-r-bonney-gabriel-is-miss-universe-2022.html |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=Pilipino Express |location=[[Winnipeg, Manitoba]] |date=January 16, 2023 |language=en-gb |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117021209/http://www.pilipino-express.com/showbiz-showbuzz/5545-r-bonney-gabriel-is-miss-universe-2022.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Her mother is from [[Beaumont, Texas|Beaumont]].<ref name=":0">{{cite news |date=September 23, 2022 |last=Maines |first=Don |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/neighborhood/bayarea/article/How-R-Bonney-Gabriel-first-Filipina-American-to-w-17462381.php |title=How R'Bonney Gabriel, first Filipina American to win Miss Texas, is readying for shot at Miss USA |website=[[Houston Chronicle]] |access-date=October 4, 2022 |archive-date=October 4, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004051115/https://www.houstonchronicle.com/neighborhood/bayarea/article/How-R-Bonney-Gabriel-first-Filipino-American-to-w-17462381.php |url-status=live }}</ref> Gabriel spent some time in [[Manila]] during her childhood playing in the streets, playing [[tong-its]], and watching the parade of [[Filipino fiestas]]. She and her family have continued to visit the Philippines during holidays and summer vacations, going back and living in Malate, on the same street where her father is from.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 16, 2023 |title=R'Bonney Gabriel reminisces on her childhood as she visits dad's home street in Manila |url=https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/lifestyle/familyandrelationships/870206/r-bonney-gabriel-reminisces-on-her-childhood-as-she-visits-dad-s-home-street-in-manila/story/ |access-date=May 18, 2023 |website=GMA News Online |language=en |archive-date=May 18, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230518034529/https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/lifestyle/familyandrelationships/870206/r-bonney-gabriel-reminisces-on-her-childhood-as-she-visits-dad-s-home-street-in-manila/story/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Gabriel graduated from the [[University of North Texas]] in 2018 with a bachelor's degree in fashion design with a minor in fibers.<ref>{{cite news |title=R'Bonney Gabriel, a UNT graduate, crowned as the new Miss Universe |url=https://www.dallasnews.com/arts-entertainment/2023/01/15/rbonney-gabriel-a-unt-graduate-crowned-as-the-new-miss-universe/ |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=[[Dallas News]] |date=January 15, 2023 |language=en |archive-date=January 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230117131800/https://www.dallasnews.com/arts-entertainment/2023/01/15/rbonney-gabriel-a-unt-graduate-crowned-as-the-new-miss-universe/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Fashion Design alumna R'Bonney Gabriel wins Miss USA 2022 |url=https://news.cvad.unt.edu/alum-gabriel-rbonney-fashion-design |website=College of Visual Arts and Design, [[University of North Texas]] |access-date=January 15, 2023 |archive-date=February 4, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204114050/https://news.cvad.unt.edu/alum-gabriel-rbonney-fashion-design |url-status=live }}</ref> She works as a designer creating [[Sustainable fashion|eco-friendly clothing]], and as a model.<ref name=":0" /> She has worked as a sewing instructor at a non-profit organization.<ref name="vogue.ph/rbonney-wins">{{cite news |last1=Perez |first1=Mariane |title=R'Bonney Gabriel Wins Miss Universe 2022 |url=https://vogue.ph/lifestyle/people/rbonney-gabriel-wins-miss-universe-2022/ |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=vogue.ph |date=January 15, 2023 |archive-date=February 3, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230203205540/https://vogue.ph/lifestyle/people/rbonney-gabriel-wins-miss-universe-2022/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Pageantry==
Gabriel's first pageant was Miss Kemah USA 2020, where she reached the top five finalists.<ref>{{cite news |date=July 31, 2020 |last=Maines |first=Don |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/neighborhood/bayarea/news/article/Clear-Falls-cheerleader-wins-Miss-Kemah-Teen-15449608.php |title=Clear Falls cheerleader wins Miss Kemah Teen |website=[[Houston Chronicle]] |access-date=October 4, 2022 |archive-date=October 4, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004045617/https://www.houstonchronicle.com/neighborhood/bayarea/news/article/Clear-Falls-cheerleader-wins-Miss-Kemah-Teen-15449608.php |url-status=live }}</ref> She competed at [[Miss Texas USA]] 2021 as Miss Harris County and was the first runner-up to Victoria Hinojosa of [[McAllen]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.misstexasusa.com/results-miss-2021/|title=Results – Miss – 2021 &#124; Miss Texas USA & Miss Texas Teen USA|access-date=January 16, 2023|archive-date=January 16, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230116083136/https://www.misstexasusa.com/results-miss-2021/|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Miss USA 2022 ===
{{Main|Miss USA 2022}}
Having won [[Miss Texas USA]] 2022, she went on to win Miss USA 2022,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.goodmorningamerica.com/culture/story/time-texas-represented-asian-american-women-miss-usa-90914537|title=For the first time, Texas represented by Asian American women in Miss USA and Miss America pageants|access-date=October 4, 2022|website=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]|publisher=[[Good Morning America]]|archive-date=October 4, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004081520/https://www.goodmorningamerica.com/amp/culture/story/time-texas-represented-asian-american-women-miss-usa-90914537|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Texas2022">{{cite web|url=https://www.khou.com/article/news/local/miss-texas-usa-2022/285-8b147fc3-93b5-4195-befe-d35520713eb4|title=First Filipina crowned Miss Texas USA|publisher=[[KHOU-TV]]|last=Diaz|first=John|date=July 4, 2022|access-date=July 4, 2022|archive-date=September 29, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220929023403/https://www.khou.com/article/news/local/miss-texas-usa-2022/285-8b147fc3-93b5-4195-befe-d35520713eb4|url-status=live}}</ref> becoming the first [[Miss USA]] of Filipino descent.<ref name="winner">{{cite web|date=October 4, 2022|url=https://www.manipursana.in/2022/10/averie-bishop-and-rbonney-gabriel-win.html?m=1|title=Averie Bishop and R'Bonney Gabriel – win Miss USA, Miss America pageant|access-date=October 4, 2022|website=ManipurSana|archive-date=October 4, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004052434/https://www.manipursana.in/2022/10/averie-bishop-and-rbonney-gabriel-win.html?m=1|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="eonline/1349398">{{cite news |title=Miss USA 2022 R'Bonney Gabriel Responds to Allegation Her Win Was "Rigged" |url=https://www.eonline.com/news/1349398/miss-usa-2022-rbonney-gabriel-responds-to-allegation-her-win-was-rigged |access-date=January 17, 2023 |work=[[E! Online]] |date=October 7, 2022 |archive-date=January 20, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230120012634/https://www.eonline.com/news/1349398/miss-usa-2022-rbonney-gabriel-responds-to-allegation-her-win-was-rigged |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=October 4, 2022 |url=https://mb.com.ph/2022/10/04/fil-am-beauty-queen-crowned-miss-usa-2022/ |title=Fil-Am beauty queen crowned Miss USA 2022 |access-date=October 4, 2022 |website=[[Manila Bulletin]] |archive-date=October 4, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004091252/https://mb.com.ph/2022/10/04/fil-am-beauty-queen-crowned-miss-usa-2022/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Gabriel became the second titleholder from [[Texas]], after [[Chelsi Smith]], to win the Miss Universe title.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Munce |first1=Megan |title=R'Bonney Gabriel of Friendswood, first Filipina Miss Texas and Miss USA, wins Miss Universe |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/article/rbonney-gabriel-miss-universe-texas-17719347.php |access-date=January 19, 2023 |work=Houston Chronicle |date=January 15, 2023 |url-access=subscription |archive-date=March 20, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230320151542/https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/article/rbonney-gabriel-miss-universe-texas-17719347.php |url-status=live }}</ref>

After the event, allegations emerged that the competition had been rigged for Gabriel to win. It was claimed that Gabriel traveled to Nizuc Resort and Spa in [[Cancún]] weeks after Gabriel was crowned Miss Texas USA and was able to shoot promotional material, which the resort's [[Instagram]] account posted less than 24 hours after the final competition. Nizuc has become one of the pageant's sponsors since national director and [[Miss USA 2008]] [[Crystle Stewart]] took over at the end of 2020 after Miss USA and [[Miss Teen USA]] were separated from the Miss Universe Organization until her suspension.<ref name="eonline/1349398" /> Both Gabriel and [[Miss Colorado USA]] Alexis Glover were not included in the official Cancún retreat along with the rest of the contestants as Texas and Colorado had not yet crowned at the time of the retreat.<ref>{{cite web |last=Kao |first=Brooke |date=October 6, 2022 |title=Contestants claim Miss USA 2022 was 'rigged': 'We were humiliated' |url=https://nypost.com/2022/10/06/contestants-claim-miss-usa-2022-pageant-was-rigged/ |access-date=October 6, 2022 |work=[[The New York Post]] |archive-date=October 13, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221013130000/https://nypost.com/2022/10/06/contestants-claim-miss-usa-2022-pageant-was-rigged/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.news.com.au/lifestyle/fashion/fashion-shows/pageant-world-implodes-amid-claims-miss-usa-was-rigged/news-story/9e6b2e63b66331021e8a96e34bbe63e4|title=Pageant world implodes amid claims Miss USA was 'rigged'}}</ref> In an interview with ''[[E! News]]'', Gabriel refuted claims that the pageant was rigged. She stated, "I would never enter any pageant or any competition that I know I would win".<ref name="eonline/1349398" />

===Miss Universe 2022===
{{Main|Miss Universe 2022}}
As Miss USA 2022, she represented the United States at the Miss Universe 2022 pageant on January 14, 2023, at the [[New Orleans Morial Convention Center]] in [[New Orleans]], Louisiana, after being postponed from late 2022 to January 2023 due to the [[2022 FIFA World Cup]]. Her national costume was based on the [[Apollo 11|1969 U.S. moon landing]]<ref>{{cite web|last=Noyen|first=Maria|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/miss-usa-wore-30-pound-moon-costume-miss-universe-pageant-2023-1|title=Miss USA wore a 30-pound woman on the moon-inspired costume that spanned over 30 inches in diameter at the Miss Universe pageant|date=January 15, 2023|website=Business Insider|access-date=November 4, 2025}}</ref>

She was crowned Miss Universe 2022 by the outgoing titleholder [[Harnaaz Sandhu]] of India, making her the ninth American to win the beauty pageant. She is also the sixth mixed-heritage woman to win the Miss Universe title after [[Chelsi Smith]] at [[Miss Universe 1995]], [[Brook Lee]] at [[Miss Universe 1997]], [[Pia Wurtzbach]] at [[Miss Universe 2015]], [[Demi-Leigh Tebow]] at [[Miss Universe 2017]], and [[Catriona Gray]] at [[Miss Universe 2018]]. She is the fifth [[Miss Universe]] of Filipino descent and the first Filipina to win Miss Universe outside the Philippines.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/lifestyle/fashion/2023/01/16/filipina-miss-universe-winners/|title=Mixed-heritage Filipina winners of Miss Universe, from R'Bonney Gabriel to Pia Wurtzbach|access-date=January 16, 2023|website=The National News|date=January 16, 2023|archive-date=June 3, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230603005326/https://www.thenationalnews.com/lifestyle/fashion/2023/01/16/filipina-miss-universe-winners/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.philstar.com/lifestyle/fashion-and-beauty/2023/01/16/2237986/we-are-very-proud-you-pia-wurtzbach-catriona-gray-send-messages-support-celeste-cortesi|title='We are very proud of you': Pia Wurtzbach, Catriona Gray send messages of support to Celeste Cortesi|access-date=January 16, 2023|website=[[The Philippine Star]]|date=January 16, 2023}}</ref> Her victory also made her the first representative from the United States to win Miss Universe since [[Olivia Culpo]] at [[Miss Universe 2012]].<ref>{{cite web|title=The moment you've been waiting for… The #71stMISSUNIVERSE Competition is heading to… NEW ORLEANS, LOUISIANA! 🇺🇸|url=https://www.instagram.com/p/CisdAxFgNqA/|website=[[Instagram]]|access-date=October 4, 2022|archive-date=October 21, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221021093032/https://www.instagram.com/p/CisdAxFgNqA/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="venue">{{cite web |last=Bracamonte |first=Earl |date=September 19, 2022 |title=Miss Universe 2022 reveals date, venue; confirms moms, wives can join |url=https://www.philstar.com/entertainment/2022/09/19/2210739/miss-universe-2022-reveals-date-venueconfirms-moms-wives-can-join |access-date=September 19, 2022 |website=[[The Philippine Star]] |language=en |archive-date=September 26, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220926170013/https://www.philstar.com/entertainment/2022/09/19/2210739/miss-universe-2022-reveals-date-venueconfirms-moms-wives-can-join |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="auto">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/lists/miss-usa-2022-winner-rbonney-gabriel-texas-wins/|title=Miss USA 2022 Winner: R'Bonney Gabriel — Miss Texas Wins|access-date=October 4, 2022|website=[[TVLine]]|date=October 4, 2022|archive-date=October 4, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221004104101/https://tvline.com/lists/miss-usa-2022-winner-rbonney-gabriel-texas-wins/|url-status=live}}</ref> She is also the first Miss Universe titleholder to be born and raised in the [[Greater Houston]] area.<ref name="auto"/> Additionally, she is the second Asian American woman to win the Miss Universe title since Brook Lee at Miss Universe 1997, and also the oldest winner at 28 years old, succeeding [[Andrea Meza]] of Mexico.

In her capacity as Miss Universe, Gabriel traveled to Indonesia,<ref>{{Cite web |last=pebri |date=February 26, 2023 |title=R'Bonney Gabriel, Miss Universe 2022 - Impressed on Bali |url=https://observerid.com/rbonney-gabriel-miss-universe-2022-impressed-on-bali/ |access-date=July 7, 2023 |website=OBSERVER |language=en-US |archive-date=July 7, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230707163002/https://observerid.com/rbonney-gabriel-miss-universe-2022-impressed-on-bali/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Thailand,<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=February 12, 2023 |title=Miss Universe 2022 R'Bonney Gabriel arrives in Thailand as part of her Asian tour |url=https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/lifestyle/hobbiesandactivities/860527/miss-universe-2022-r-bonney-gabriel-arrives-in-thailand-as-part-of-her-asian-tour/story/ |access-date=February 17, 2023 |website=GMA News Online |language=en |archive-date=February 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230217231206/https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/lifestyle/hobbiesandactivities/860527/miss-universe-2022-r-bonney-gabriel-arrives-in-thailand-as-part-of-her-asian-tour/story/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Malaysia, Vietnam,<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |title=Báo VietnamNet |url=https://vietnamnet.vn/en/miss-universe-2022-explores-vietnamese-culture-2114855.html |access-date=July 7, 2023 |website=VietNamNet News |language=vietnamese |archive-date=July 7, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230707162918/https://vietnamnet.vn/en/miss-universe-2022-explores-vietnamese-culture-2114855.html |url-status=live }}</ref> the Philippines,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tusing |first=David |date=May 11, 2023 |title=Miss Universe R'Bonney Gabriel in the Philippines for the first time since her win |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/lifestyle/fashion-beauty/2023/05/11/miss-universe-rbonney-gabriel-in-the-philippines-for-the-first-time-since-her-win/ |access-date=July 7, 2023 |website=The National |language=en |archive-date=July 7, 