'''Juan Daniel Fernández Molero''' (born July 22, 1987) is a Peruvian [[Filmmaking|filmmaker]]. He is known for his [[avant-garde]] films ''[[Reminiscences (2010 film)|Reminiscences]]'' (2010), ''[[Videophilia (and Other Viral Syndromes)]]'' (2015), which won the Tiger Award at the [[International Film Festival Rotterdam]], and ''[[Punku]]'' (2025), which premiered in the Forum section at the [[75th Berlin International Film Festival]].

== Career ==
Fernández was born in [[Lima]] in 1987, he studied for two years at the University of Cinema in Buenos Aires (FUC), was a student in the Trainee Project for Young Film Critics of the [[Rotterdam Film Festival]], and in the Talent Campus of Buenos Aires (2010) and the [[Berlinale]] (2011).<ref>{{Cite web |title=Juan Daniel F. Molero |url=http://cinelatinoamericano.org/cineasta.aspx?cod=5572 |access-date=2026-05-18 |website=Cine Latinoamericano}}</ref>

In 2008, he founded Tiempo Libre, a film production company through which he also distributes films in cultural circuits and organizes film workshops.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Punku |url=https://festivaldelima.com/2025/pelicula/punku/ |website=[[Lima Film Festival]]}}</ref>

In 2009, F. Molero collected old recordings and home video archives to create ''[[Reminiscences (2010 film)|Reminiscences]]'', a documentary feature exploring the creation and loss of memory based on his own episode of amnesia following a sandboarding accident. A short version premiered in July of that year at the Centro Cultural Cafae.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Campos |first=John |title=Entrevista: Juan Daniel Fernández y sus «Reminiscencias» |url=https://www.cinencuentro.com/2010/04/29/entrevista-juan-daniel-fernandez-reminiscencias/ |access-date=2026-05-18 |website=Cinencuentro}}</ref> The following year, an extended version premiered in March at the 25th [[Guadalajara International Film Festival]].<ref name="Cinencuentro">{{cite news|last=Gómez|first=John Campos|title=Entrevista: Juan Daniel Fernández y sus "Reminiscencias"|language=Spanish|url=http://www.cinencuentro.com/2010/04/29/entrevista-juan-daniel-fernandez-reminiscencias/|accessdate=December 11, 2011|newspaper=Cinencuentro|date=April 29, 2010}}</ref>

In 2015, he premiered his first feature film, ''[[Videophilia (and Other Viral Syndromes)]]'', which won the Tiger Award at the [[International Film Festival Rotterdam]],<ref>{{Cite web|date=2015-02-03|title=Peru and Cuba Win Big at the Rotterdam Film Festival's Tiger Awards|url=https://remezcla.com/film/peru-cuba-win-big-rotterdam-film-festivals-tiger-awards/|access-date=2022-01-18|website=Remezcla|language=en-US}}</ref> becoming the first Peruvian film to win the festival's top prize.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rojas |first=Laslo |title=Entrevista con el director de «Videofilia», Juan Daniel F. Molero: la vida real también es virtual |url=https://www.cinencuentro.com/2015/06/22/pelicula-peruana-videofilia-entrevista-juan-daniel-f-molero/ |access-date=2026-05-18 |website=Cinencuentro}}</ref> Subsequently, it was selected as the Peruvian entry for the [[Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film|Best Foreign Language Film]] at the [[89th Academy Awards]].<ref name="Peru">{{cite web|url=http://www.entornointeligente.com/articulo/8942055/PERU-Oscar-2017-la-pelicula-Videofilia-representara-al-Peru|title=PERÚ: Oscar 2017: la película "Videofilia" representará al Perú|work=Entorno Inteligente|date=15 September 2016|access-date=15 September 2016}}</ref>

In 2025, he released his second feature film, ''[[Punku]]'', in the Forum section at the [[75th Berlin International Film Festival]],<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2025-02-15 |title=Cineasta peruano invita en la Berlinale con "Punku" a transitar entre realidad y sueño |url=https://www.infobae.com/america/agencias/2025/02/15/cineasta-peruano-invita-en-la-berlinale-con-punku-a-transitar-entre-realidad-y-sueno/ |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=Infobae |language=es-ES}}</ref> nominated for the [[International Federation of Film Critics|FIPRESI Prize]] in that section,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Roxborough |first=Scott |date=2025-02-22 |title=Berlin: Fipresci International Film Critic Award Winners |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/berlin2025-fipresci-international-film-critics-award-winners-1236143761/ |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> also was nominated for the [[Trophy Spondylus]] at the [[29th Lima Film Festival]],<ref>{{cite web |date=24 July 2025 |title=Toda la programación del Festival de Cine de Lima 2025 |url=https://www.escribiendocine.com/noticias/2025/07/24/20099-toda-la-programacion-del-festival-de-cine-de-lima-2025 |accessdate=18 August 2025 |website=Escribiendo Cine |language=es}}</ref> winning Best Cinematography - Special Mention for Johan Carrasco.<ref>{{Cite web |title=¡Estos son los ganadores del 29 Festival de Cine de Lima PUCP! |url=https://festivaldelima.com/2025/estos-son-los-ganadores-del-29-festival-de-cine-de-lima-pucp/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250819150503/https://festivaldelima.com/2025/estos-son-los-ganadores-del-29-festival-de-cine-de-lima-pucp/ |archive-date=August 19, 2025 |access-date=August 16, 2025 |website=[[Lima Film Festival|festivaldelima.com]]}}</ref>

