'''Alizée Minard''' (born 6 May 1997) is a French [[Javelin throw|javelin]] thrower. She is a multiple-time French national champion.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/athletes/france/alizee-minard-14595849 |title=Alizée MINARD |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref>

==Biography==
As a junior athlete, she competed in [[pole vault]], winning age-group regional titles in [[Aquitaine]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.sudouest.fr/landes/capbreton/des-athletes-d-exception-10087758.php |first=Bruno |last=Magnes |title=Exceptional athletes |website=sudouest.fr |date=18 August 2010 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.sudouest.fr/landes/capbreton/un-hiver-prolifique-8697564.php |first=Bruno |last=Magnes |title=A prolific winter : The club continues to develop its young players |website=sudouest.fr |date=13 March 2013 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.sudouest.fr/landes/capbreton/le-beau-final-des-athletes-7747573.php |first=Bruno |last=Magnes |title=Le beau final des athlètes |website=sudouest.fr |date=12 June 2015 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref> She was later a member of Club Athlétique Balmanais and focused on the [[javelin throw]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.ladepeche.fr/2023/06/27/les-athletes-ont-performe-en-pologne-11303734.php# |date=27 June 2023 |title=Balma. Les athlètes ont performé en Pologne |website=La Depeche |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref>

Competing for [[Arizona State University]] and trained in the javelin throw by coach [[Brian Blutreich]], she won the 2021 PAC-12 Championships, and finished as runner-up at the [[2021 NCAA Division I Outdoor Track and Field Championships|2021 NCAA Championships]] with a throw of 57.91 metres, although a partially torn UCL in her elbow limited her to only four competitions in the United States that year.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7155000?eventId=10229533 |title=NCAA Div. I Outdoor Championships |date=9 June 2021 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.statepress.com/article/2021/07/spsports-alizee-minard-asu-track-and-field-javelin-ncaa-pac-12-champion |website=statepress.com |title=An injury cut Alizée Minard's sole season to four meets. She still set ASU records |date=30 June 2021 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref> Later that summer, she finished as runner-up at the [[2021 French Athletics Championships]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.ladepeche.fr/2021/06/26/jona-aigouy-decroche-le-titre-national-9632651.php# |title=Millau. French Athletics Championships : Millau native Jöna Aigouy wins the national title |website=La Dépêche du Midi |date=26 June 2021 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7168687?eventId=10229533 |title=French Championships |date=25 June 2021 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref>

Minard won the javelin at the [[2022 French Athletics Championships]] in [[Caen]], with a throw of 57.17 metres.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7186790?eventId=10229533 |title=French Championships |date=24 June 2022 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref> She won the bronze medal at the [[Athletics at the 2022 Mediterranean Games|2022 Mediterranean Games]], moving into the medal positions with her final throw of the competition. She represented France at the [[2022 European Athletics Championships]] in Germany.<ref>{{cite web |title=Balma. Alizée Minard : le rêve en bleu est devenu réalité |url=https://www.ladepeche.fr/2022/07/11/alizee-minard-le-reve-en-bleu-est-devenu-realite-10428336.php |website=La Dépêche du Midi |date=11 July 2022 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Athletics – Alizée Minard: When I say I do javelin, I hear "is that the thing with the pole vault?" |access-date=29 June 2026 |url=https://sans-filtre.fr/athle-alizee-minard-quand-je-dis-que-je-fais-du-javelot-jentends-cest-le-truc-avec-la-perche/#google_vignette |date=29 August 2022 |website=Sans-Filtre.fr}}</ref>

In February 2023, she won the French Winter Throwing Championships in [[Salon-de-Provence]], with a throw of 53.80 metres.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.athle.fr/actualites/championnats-de-france-hivernaux-de-lancers-guehaseim-en-veut-plus/18904 |title=French Winter Throwing Championships: Guehaseim wants more |date=27 February 2023 |website=Athle.fr |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref> In June 2023, she placed tenth overall representing France at the [[2023 European Athletics Team Championships First Division]] in Poland.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.athle.fr/contenu/championnats-d-europe-par-equipes-2023-chorzow-pol-zeze-kpatcha-meniker-ont-mene-la-remontee/6624 |website=Athle.fr |access-date=29 June 2026 |title=Zézé, Kpatcha and Meniker led the comeback}}</ref>

In June 2024, Minard won the javelin at the French Athletics Championships in [[Angers]], with a throw of 55.95 metres.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7205979?eventId=10229533 |title=French Championships |date=28 June 2024 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref> That month, she won the National de Strasbourg meeting ahead of Asian champion [[Annu Rani]], with a throw of 57.77 metres.<ref>{{cite web |website=Olympics.com |url=https://www.olympics.com/en/news/annu-rani-javelin-throw-india-strasbourg-athletics-meet-2024-results |title=Annu Rani finishes second in javelin throw at Strasbourg athletics meet |date=9 June 2024 |access-date=29 June 2026}}</ref>

Minard placed sixth overall at the [[2025 European Athletics Team Championships First Division]] in [[Madrid]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7173259?eventId=10229533 |title=European Athletics Team Championships First Division |date=29 June 2025 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref> She retained her national title by winning the javelin throw at the 2025 French Athletics Championships in [[Talence]], with a personal best throw of 60.65 metres to finish ahead of [[Jade Maraval]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7226084?eventId=10229533 |title=French Championships |date=2 August 2025 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Le Baron, Minard, Petit… 5 French athletes who could break out in 2026 |first=Etienne |last=Goursaud |date=5 January 2026 |access-date=29 June 2026 |url=https://dicodusport.fr/blog/le-baron-minard-petit-5-athletes-francais-qui-peuvent-se-reveler-en-2026/ |website=Dicodu Sport}}</ref>

Minard threw a new personal best of 61.51 metres to place fourth overall at the [[2026 Meeting de Paris]], part of the [[2026 Diamond League]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7214022?eventId=10229533 |title=Meeting de Paris |date=28 June 2026 |access-date=28 June 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref> On 24 July, she threw a new personal best and championship record 61.69 metres to win the French Championships.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://dicodusport.fr/blog/kpatcha-black-minard-les-quatre-temps-forts-de-la-1re-journee-des-championnats-de-france-dathletisme-2026/ |website=Dicodusport.fr |title=ATHLÉTISME Kpatcha, Black, Minard… Les quatre temps forts de la 1re journée des championnats de France d’athlétisme 2026 |first=Etienne |last=Goursaud |date=24 July 2026 |access-date=25 July 2026}}</ref> In August, she competed at the [[2026 European Athletics Championships – Women's javelin throw| 2026 European Athletics Championships]] in Birmingham, England, in the javelin throw, placing fifth overall.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://worldathletics.org/competition/calendar-results/results/7192415?eventId=10229533&gender=W |title=European Athletics Championships |date=10 August 2026 |access-date=19 August 2026 |website=World Athletics}}</ref>

